<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zōthēca</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωθήκη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little private chamber</i>, <i>closet</i>, or <i>cabinet</i>, for reposing in
			by day (cf. conclave), <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 2, 17, 21</span></i>; cf.
			zothecula.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A recess</i>, <i>niche</i>, for
			religious purposes, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			1368</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2006</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3889</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
